{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And it shall be.</b> The host of the Chaldeans:" "<b>Like a driven gazelle.</b> That the pursuers drive it [i.e., use the hif'il of the root דוח]. It is a pu'al participle of the heavy [i.e., geminate] binyan, on the pattern of מוקטר [Malachi 1:11], מוגש [ibid.], מוצב ארצה (Genesis 28:12):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:36.911973723Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}